    "narrative": "The **Gunnar Henderson** matchup against Kremer remains the premier play for the Austin Waves today, anchoring the lineup with a stellar 79.74 efficiency score. His promotion to the leadoff spot paired with a favorable platoon advantage provides the highest ceiling for run production in our current rotation. **Jacob Wilson** also enters \"Strong\" territory (66.55) despite the presence of Peralta on the mound; the projected shift to the two-hole provides enough volume to offset the difficulty of the opposing pitcher. **Kyle Tucker** (63.91) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.95) provide essential stability in the heart of the order, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** specifically benefiting from a park factor boost that keeps him firmly in the lineup despite a slightly tougher matchup against Gray.\n\nWe are navigating a volatile board with significant \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key pieces, necessitating caution with **Wade Meckler** (42.35) and **Luis Lara** (42.99). Both currently sit at the bottom of our start threshold due to platoon sensitivities and middling SP matchups. The toughest bench decision involved balancing **Andy Pages** (60.44) against our corner infield depth; while **Andy Pages** earned the start due to his projected #2 spot and high sprint speed profile\u2014critical for our focus on scarce stolen bases\u2014he narrowly edged out internal depth options like **Miguel Vargas** or **Curtis Mead**, who failed to clear the 60-point threshold against today\u2019s projected arms.\n\nStrategic caution is advised regarding **Drake Baldwin**, whose 54.36 score is tethered to a 31% rain risk; if the weather deteriorates in his matchup against Scott, we risk burning a daily game cap on a shortened outing. Furthermore, while **Jackson Merrill** is active, he faces the toughest opposing pitcher on the slate in Henderson (2.82 xERA). We remain sidelined for the foreseeable future on **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** due to injury status, and our bench remains heavy with utility options like **Sam Antonacci** and **Dominic Smith** who are currently outside the daily efficiency window. We are monitoring **Heliot Ramos** closely, but he remains on the periphery as we prioritize high-speed, high-OBP leadoff threats to maximize our 5x5 categorical output.",
